==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is a [[Corrupted Cat Base (Enemy Base)|Corrupted Cat Base]].
*Infinite [[Killer Cat (Enemy)|Killer Cats]] spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 120 seconds<sup>3,600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Killer Cat (Enemy)|Killer Cat]] spawns.
**45 [[Killer Cat (Enemy)|Killer Cats]] spawn, delay 1.33~2 seconds<sup>40f~60f</sup>.
**30 [[Killer Cat (Enemy)|Killer Cats]] spawn, delay 2.67~4 seconds<sup>80f~120f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The real deal of the event... massively buffed Killer Cats come in humongous stacks to plow down your army. An extreme challenge without [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] and [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|dual]] [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Erasers]] or [[Nono (Rare Cat)|Nono]]. Kill the Killer Cats as fast as possible before they kill you, but don't get too close to the enemy base unless you're ready to destroy it. If you do, it will fire a cannon blast with enough power to kill almost all of your meatshields and attackers. If you do not use at least 3-4 meatshields, the Killer Cats will easily get through them, destroy your base, and you will lose. Use highly damaging [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area Attackers]] like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] or [[:Category:Anti-Dark Cats|anti-Dark]]s like [[Talents|Talented]] [[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Heavy Assault C.A.T]], [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Ring Girl Cat]], or any other heavy hitters to kill the Killer Cats. If you manage to survive the onslaught, then victory is yours!

==Trivia==
*The 222 Incident is a reference to the [[wikipedia:February 26 Incident|2-26 Incident]], an attempted coup d'état in the Empire of Japan on 26 February 1936.

